.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL>
.br
class csmp::ModelSubDomain< dim, CELL >"Storage of \fBNode\fP and \fBCell\fP pointers to subdomains of the overall computational model\&. Distinguishes interior from perimeter nodes (located on subdomain boundary) and interior and perimeter cells which have at least a single \fBFace\fP on the subdomain boundary\&. \fBBase\fP class to \fBRegion\fP, \fBBoundary\fP and \fBSplitBoundary\fP\&. 


.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
\fBRegion\fP, Bounday, \fBSplitBoundary\fP ARE AGNOSTIC ABOUT MESH CONNECTIVITY\&. \fBModelSubDomain\fP objects do not create Nodes, Elements, Faces or Interfaces\&. This is the role of the \fBMeshManager\fP that is agnostic about subdomains but maintains and updates the mesh\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBBoundary\fP and SplitBoundare are \fBModelSubDomain\fP subclasses consisting of lower-dimensional \fBFace\fP and \fBInterFace\fP objects\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
SplitBoundaries are Internal boundaries connecting node-matched but disconnected mesh patches
.IP "\(bu" 2
Boundaries tend to be external boundaries with names corresponding to the sides of box-shaped models or other unique names\&. 
.PP
.RE
.PP

