.PP
The two string arguments define the name of the node property which is interpolated and the name of the cell property to which the interpolated value is written\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
This method was developed for two-dimensional convection calculations where the fluid density as cell property must be exactly the same for in the two adjacent triangles which make up a square in regular-gridded meshes\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
